---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WaveEdge from '../components/WaveEdge.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="XUGA gives worn-out beach towels a second life as island wear, and a voice through Towel Tales."
>
  <section class="px-5 pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="font-hand text-2xl text-[var(--accent)]">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-1 font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        We give beach towels a second life, and a voice.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-5 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">Why towels</h2>
      <p>
        Beach towels wear out quickly. They go thin in the middle, the colours
        fade, the edges fray, and most are thrown away while the fabric still
        has years of life left in it. XUGA is a student-led island-wear brand
        in {SITE.place}. We take those towels and sew them, by hand and one at
        a time, into bucket hats, shorts, belt bags and pouches.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because every towel is different, every piece is different. There is
        no second copy. There cannot be.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-sand-deep px-5 py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">Why a tale</h2>
      <p>
        A second-hand towel carries a history that most upcycled fashion
        quietly throws away. We thought that history was worth keeping. So
        every XUGA piece is sewn with a small tag, and every tag opens a page
        where the towel itself tells you where it has been: the summers, the
        beaches, the hotel by the sea, the person who decided not to bin it.
      </p>
      <p>
        It makes the piece feel like yours, because it is the only one of its
        kind, and now you know its whole story.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-5 py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">Honest about the green part</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell vague promises. The eco figures on each tale are
        estimates, worked out from the weight of the towel and the average
        impact of producing new cotton, and we label them as estimates every
        time. The real point is simpler than any number: a towel that becomes
        a garment is a towel that did not become waste.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-ink px-5 py-16 text-sand">
    <WaveEdge color="var(--color-sand)" />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl">Say hello</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-md text-sand/70">
        XUGA is made by students in {SITE.place}. If you have a towel with a
        story, or just want to see what we are making next, come and find us.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2 text-sand">
        <li>
          <a
            class="underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
            href={SITE.instagram.url}>Instagram {SITE.instagram.handle}</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            class="underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
            href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/contact/"
            >Get in touch</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
